{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511164-arikel","id":1511164,"title":"Arikel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-09T16:46:48-07:00","id":1511164,"title":"Arikel","content":"The seductress ancient vampire Blood Goddess is honestly one of my favorite character archetypes (Akasha, Neferata, etc) so I find quite dissapointing the lack of content she has compared to Tzimisce, Saulot or Malkav for example.<br /> <br /> And by this I don't mean stuff like &quot;I want to know all the details about her&quot; but all we have right now is &quot;She is probably chill and the most well-behaved ante... or not&quot; which is kinda lame tbh. Mostly because it is basically player generated, not because we have any implication that she is or isn't. We have some myths of her being chill, a mention of her being a councillor so we kinda assume maybe she is and the possibility she isn't comes &quot;She is master of presence and auspex&quot;<br /> <br /> I would like if her (and Ventru for that matter) got some love. Some update, some fan of possibilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26553-hera-stan-account","name":"Hera Stan Account","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T17:12:03-07:00","id":1511166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hera Stan Account</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511164-arikel#post1511164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The seductress ancient vampire Blood Goddess is honestly one of my favorite character archetypes (Akasha, Neferata, etc) so I find quite dissapointing the lack of content she has compared to Tzimisce, Saulot or Malkav for example.<br /> <br /> And by this I don't mean stuff like &quot;I want to know all the details about her&quot; but all we have right now is &quot;She is probably chill and the most well-behaved ante... or not&quot; which is kinda lame tbh. Mostly because it is basically player generated, not because we have any implication that she is or isn't. We have some myths of her being chill, a mention of her being a councillor so we kinda assume maybe she is and the possibility she isn't comes &quot;She is master of presence and auspex&quot;<br /> <br /> I would like if her (and Ventru for that matter) got some love. Some update, some fan of possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I'm not mistaken, it's not confirmed if Arikel is a &quot;she&quot;, not that it means anything hahaha...<br /> <br /> To be fair, Tremere, Capadocius/Ashur and Saulot and Tzimisce got the most &quot;screen time&quot; by far among the Antediluvians, Malkav ,IIRC is only &quot;present&quot; in <b>Fountains of Bright Crimson</b>.<br /> In any case, I agree with you that he/she is a little &quot;too absent&quot; from the stories of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-09T17:55:40-07:00","id":1511168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hera Stan Account</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511164-arikel#post1511164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The seductress ancient vampire Blood Goddess is honestly one of my favorite character archetypes (Akasha, Neferata, etc) so I find quite dissapointing the lack of content she has compared to Tzimisce, Saulot or Malkav for example.<br /> <br /> And by this I don't mean stuff like &quot;I want to know all the details about her&quot; but all we have right now is &quot;She is probably chill and the most well-behaved ante... or not&quot; which is kinda lame tbh. Mostly because it is basically player generated, not because we have any implication that she is or isn't. We have some myths of her being chill, a mention of her being a councillor so we kinda assume maybe she is and the possibility she isn't comes &quot;She is master of presence and auspex&quot;<br /> <br /> I would like if her (and Ventru for that matter) got some love. Some update, some fan of possibilities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this doesn't replace it, but I've learned a few minor details about him or her, now making it clear that I've heard it, so I don't know the source material. What I do know is that she is somehow connected with the myth of the minotaur, as it is mentioned that King Minos was directly embraced by her and his son was embraced afterwards, the reason I do not know. Another thing they overlook is that one of the Sirens myths is mentioned that she and Malkav were close and some stipulate, I think this is fanfic, that the two were and maybe still are lovers. Other than that, all I know is that she had a private conversation with Absimiliard at some point after the flood, the exact moment I don't know. It's loose information, I know. If you want a guess, I think the writers just didn't have much to do with her since her curse didn't grant her a quirk or discipline that could be used in the apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T00:14:35-07:00","id":1511195,"title":"","content":"Thhe Toreador Antediluvian is a funny thing<br /> First, becasue possibly there was two. not one of them<br /> Of<b> Arikel, the Sculptor</b>, the twin of Malkav (and Malakai) we had some information. But not much. The Toreador can't even agree in the gender, she was probably a male tho'<br /> In DAV: Road of Humanity, the Prodigals told of a story in which Arikel and Troile were troubled by the way the Cainites of the First City behaved, and turned to Saulot for aid. The Healer stated that only empathy would help them retain a link to humanity and so, both Troile and Arikel went to work on a project of art that spanned a hundred and one years, before they brought it before Caine. The work inspired exactly those emotions within the audience that they had inspired in the mortal population. Caine was deeply touched by it and called Arikel and Troile to his side, forgiving them past trespasses. These prodigals hold this as the origin of the Road of Humanity<br /> According Clan Book: Baali, among his brethren, Nergal was the one most adept at dealing with other Cainites. It is said that he served as Arikel's wench, debated philosophy with Troile and traded vice secrets with the Tzimisce Antediluvian<br /> Revised Toreador and Ventrue Clanbooks told us, that she was killed by the Nosferatu and Setite Antediluvians, who cut out and ate her heart<br /> Minor inconvenience it seems, since she - as Clanbook: Ventrue Revised mentions - had awakened from Torpor around 260 BCE, acting as an advisor to Alchias, the Malkavian prince of Syracuse<br /> According the Nosferatu (and Transylcania Chronicles) Absimilliard and Arikel were blood bond lovers. Absimilliard had spent a long time in torpor at Enoch. After torpor, the Toreador say that he and Arikel met in 2nd century Rome.<br /> Beckett's Jyhad Diary is the last info about Arikel; Beckett, deep within a pit under a ruins in Ketef Hinnom lost himself to the madness afflicting the Malkavians. While affected he said and wrote the following quotes: &quot;Malkav. Malakai. Arikel. Lilith. Children and mother. Mekhet is free and Malakai follows\u200b&quot; (According to the Tzimisce Clan, Mekhet was a sibling of the Eldest (and thus possibly another childe of Ynosh/Enoch) who, with the Brujah antediluvian &quot;played shadow games with mortals, delighting in their own cunning and agendas&quot;. Assamite lore states that Mekhet was a great liar. The &quot;Fair is Foul&quot; scenario in Gehenna features Mekhet as one of the Apostates, Antediluvians who never entered into the Jyhad and who allied with Lilith against Caine. Here, Mekhet is a potent pre-Egyptian blood magician whose body resembles that of a mummified Samedi)<br /> Her &quot;canon&quot; line consist Amarantha (who was mistakenly diablerized by an Assamite judge while he was administering punishment to her. Amarantha's name is one of the possible sources of the word amaranth, the traditional word for diablerie. After her death, there was a cult named the Amaranthan started by her childer as revenge by diablerizing the said same Assamite judge. Her descendants still practice their activities and belief to hunt and devour Diablerists.- more about her in Clanbook: Assamite Revised, and Children of The Blood, Cults of the Blood Gods), Mi-ka-il (aka. Beshter aka. the Archangel of Constantinople, Michael) and Iontius aka. Derrick Zeel (an ancient Toreador methusela who somehow gained the ability to feed off his victims through sex rather than by normal vampiric means. - more about him in Clanbook: Toreador, Encyclopaedia Vampirica, Beckett's Jyhad Diary, and DAV: France by Night)<br /> And Minos (the sire of Helena. He was diablerised by his childe) Yezidian refugees from the remains of the Aral Sea refer to the force of ontological evil as &quot;Minos, who is the son of Arikel&quot;, who rests deep within the salt flats of the dried out sea.<br /> Our other contander is according to the Toreador revised clanbook, as told by Katherine of Montpelier, <b>Ishtar, the Bull-dancer</b> She was a mortal who lived in the City of Ubar. Perhaps it was her beauty that led to her Embrace. Thus, she became Antediluvian of the Clan of the Blossom by the time Ubar was renamed the City of Enoch. After the Deluge destroyed Enoch, the Antediluvians rebelled against their sires. \u2014 Caine's childer, the Second Generation \u2014 who they are said to have killed. Thus, Caine returned to the Antediluvians, who at the time resided in the Second City, to curse them. According to the Toreador, Caine cursed all the Antediluvians, except for Ishtar, whom he believed was innocent in the matter.<br /> Fearing possible vengeance from her angry siblings, Ishtar left the Second City to reside in Sumer. The people worshiped her beauty and made her their goddess. She also came to have a lover whom she embraced, that was known as Tammuz.<br /> Ennoia and Ishtar had a little history, The Toreador claim that Caine cursed all the Antediluvians, except for Ishtar, who remained utterly beautiful. Caine believed that she was not involved in the murder of his childer. His mercy on Toreador outraged all of her kindred siblings, in particular, Ennoia who had been cursed as &quot;the Beast&quot;. Not to mention Ennoia possessed the Tablet of Destiny until Ishtar tried to take the item from her. Outraged by this action, Ennoia set out to kill the Toreador Antediluvian.<br /> As Ennoia tracked Ishtar to Sumer, she embraced Ereshkigal to help her in the attack on her sibling. When the Gangrel came to confront Ishtar, Tammuz interceded, and ultimately gave his unlife so that Ishtar could flee. She then sought aid from the king of Sumer, Gilgamesh. However, he had already been embraced by Ennoia. The Toreador fled from the pair, but not before unleashing upon them some great monster known as the Bull of Heaven, while she escaped to Crete.(interesingly, according to the Garou, Gilgamesh was offered unlife by vampires, but was talked out of it by a Child of Gaia named Siduri Sabitu. It is said that Gilgamesh was the first human to organize resistance against vampiric rule and the Garou tell that the inborn suspicion against the undead stems from his early influence. But the two story not contradict each other; it is possible Gilgamesh indeed resisted... but finally gave in)<br /> In Crete, Ishtar resided with King Minos, who desired and demanded her gift. Initially, she refused, but then compromised to embrace his son. Unworthy of the embrace, the son fell into the clutches of the Beast. His erratic behavior had him imprisoned by his father Minos, in what was an underground maze. There, he was fed &quot;tribute&quot;, such as maidens, to squelch his hunger. Over time, the son became the fabled &quot;Minotaur&quot; who was killed by a mortal known as Theseus<br /> The Minotaur is another interesting one. Either the earliest record account of a Cainite in an extreme path of Wassail to become a Wight after an embrace... or according Werewolf, it was the last Apis who want insane. So again, the two story not really contradict each other; it is possible Ishtar managed to embrace an Apis, and her spwan was an Apis Abomination. Ouch<br /> But Minos also recieved the Embrace... just not from Ishtar, but Arikel a bit late (after Ishtar left probably)<br /> So Ishar's line is Tamuz (Clanbook: Toreador Revised) and the Minotaur.<br /> Ishtar, like Arikel leaves the scene in this point, nothing about them untill the Gehenna...<br /> Except maybe, the Laibon Legacy, called the the Ishtarri. They claim to be descended from the Babylonian goddess Ishtar, andlack the personal connection with Africa. The Ishtarri are the only Laibon Legacy that are not native to Africa; however, through manipulation and diplomacy, they have become an important part of Laibon culture. (The original outline for Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom confirms that the Ishtarri are intended to be a Toreador bloodline. The Ishtarri seem to have a combination of the weaknesses of the Toreador and Ravnos clans. Like the Ravnos, the Ishtarri each have a vice that they absolutely must indulge, lest it drive them mad. However, such vices focus on the beautiful and/or sensual, giving them something in common with the Toreador. Their Disciplines are: Celerity, Fortitude, Presence)<br /> <br /> Different Antediluvians? Perhaps, I like the idea, a Clan not necessarily have to be from one source. Even the Nosferatu toyed this with the broodmate of Absimilliard, Lucien. Only mentioned in Gehenna tho' Lucian is a supernaturally handsome man who effectively leads the Apostates under Lilith. It is suggested that he is in some way related to the Nosferatu: he may have shared a mortal parent or Second Generation sire with Absimiliard, or he may be the true Antediluvian of the Nosferatu, or the founder of a supposed Nosferatu bloodline such as the Nictuku or the Guruhi. The Guruhi itself is interesting and somewhat support a common ancestor; the Guruhi seem to share a weakness with Clan Nosferatu, though theirs is much more complicated. The appearance of a Guruhi changes based on their moods, reflected by their Orun and Aye; a Guruhi in a good mood with high Orun appears normal or may even possess unearthly beauty. However, one with a low Aye is revealed as a monstrous creature, much like the Nosferatu.Their Disciplines are: Animalism, Potence, Presence. But the original outline of Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom confirms the Guruhi are intended to be a Nosferatu bloodline.<br /> The interesting part?<br /> The Guruhi are mostly unified, despite an old legend which says there are two &quot;lines&quot; of Guruhi. The second line was supposed to take over Africa, replacing the original line when it was deemed &quot;unfit&quot;. This division is mostly forgotten and rarely taken seriously, except by a few Guruhi fanatics.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, back to Arikel and Ishtar<br /> I think it is up to the ST they are the same, they are different, or what was their fate... a bit of creative freedom<br /> Like with the Ventrue Antediluvian<br /> The official version according to clan Ventrue members states that he may have been destroyed outside of the walls of the Second City. Blaming the Brujah Antediluvian - strangely, the Brujah denying this...<br /> The porblem is:<br /> Those 4th Gen Ventrue who running around, not the mention the whole Danava Bloodline (actually I think its true they are the &quot;True Ventrue... the Ven-True... ouch, sorry, had too. And the &quot;Ventrue&quot; are an errant bloodline of Clan Danava) who claim, they are protecting the sleeping Antediluvian who they call &quot;Veddartha&quot; (and there is a Veddartha, the Younger, like Hardestat who sired Maltheas and who is an Iconnu)<br /> Artemis Orthia was embraced around 5000 BC like Medon, her broodmate, so with a bit of a strech she and her &quot;brother&quot; fits in the 2nd City death story<br /> But then it becomes... murky at best<br /> Around 3000 BC the dead Antediluvian Embraced Arakur of Ur in ancient Summer<br /> Mithras was sired in 1258 BC somewhere in the territory where Iran is now located (by Veddartha. Maybe he diablerised his way, maybe it was the Antediluvian, who know? But for the sake of argument, because there is nothing except Maltheas's sire that question this, Veddartha indeed could be the Antediluvian, while there is Veddartha, the Younger, possible the progeny of Veddartha the Elder, aka. Ventrue Antediluvian. Would be logicall, really...)<br /> Around 700 BC he embraced Alexander in Ancient Greece<br /> Before 480 BC the Antediluvian - dead, remember since the 2nd City... - embraced Tinia, who would come to rule over the Etruscans.<br /> And lastly, before 60 BC he embraced Antonius and Erik Eigermann in Ancient Gaul. Erik Eigermann and his descendants later ruled over Berlin. Antonius and his family ruled over Constantinople.<br /> Nefer-meri-Isis, the monitor of the Followers of Set (given her name, she probably originated in Egypt) was Embraced... well we don't know exactly when, but Elihu aka. Elias Andronicus, her children died in 1450 CE, so her embrace must have been before that... not much of a help, so she is not much of a proof for a living antediluvian. But even if we put her Embrace around 3000 or 5000 BC still counts somewhat, like Artemis<br /> With Presence and Dominate its easy to convince others, &quot;yeah, our Antediluvian died *sob sob* at the Walls of the 2nd City, that darn Brujah Antediluvian killed him! Never forgive! Never forget! Err... don't mind Antonius... nor the rest. They are... look, just stare that pritty picture, okay? Good lad!&quot;<br /> Really, anyone belives the Ventrue Antediluvian died in the Second City, when every Ventrue produly trace and list back their liniage to one of his children (and those Childrens were Embraced after the 2nd City where he suposedly died?)?<br /> Then again, the Lasombra belived they destroyed their Antediluvian... despite the fact, no one saw Gratiano commiting the deed, not fell in to deep slumber, still around and the Archbishop of Rio de Janeiro or jumped Generation (even if he for some reason not lowered his generation to 3rd, and became the &quot;new Antediluvian&quot; like Augustus or Tremere, its a minor miracle no one in the Sabbat wondered... gee... maybe who was Embraced 1130 CE by an Antedliuvian is probably now considered something we are fingting against...? Burn the mfker!!!), and no one in the team were capable to recall what exactly happened in there...<br /> Dominate.. fun lil' Discipline...\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-10-2023, 03:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:13:25-07:00","id":1511406,"title":"","content":"It would be very good if the Toreador Founder received more chapters and descriptions that would be about Arikel, her followers, friends, and allies. Her objectives, methods, phillosophies, wisdom, goals, and priorities could also be described and detailed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511164-arikel?p=1511166#post1511166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I'm not mistaken, it's not confirmed if Arikel is a &quot;she&quot;, not that it means anything hahaha...</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<a href=\"https://ibb.co/S35hWbJ\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/S35hWbJ</a> <br /> <br /> This picture is certainly intricate and impressive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:36:21-07:00","id":1511410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200b<a href=\"https://ibb.co/S35hWbJ\" target=\"_blank\">https://ibb.co/S35hWbJ</a><br /> <br /> This picture is certainly intricate and impressive.\u200b </div> </div> </div>Quite impressive indeed.<br /> <br /> Thanks <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> for making such a great compilation of information regarding Arikel, in its different iterations and some other Antediluvians. Really nice work, reminded me of many things I had forgotten.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T15:32:22-07:00","id":1511660,"title":"","content":"I think that definitely it would be good and worthwhile if additional descriptions, details, and stories about at least some of the Clan Founders ( or 3rd Generation Founders ) would be written.<br /> <br /> Particular books and supplements - for example books that would be specifically about history and mythology of Vampires, or cults and guilds, and maybe extended plans or projects, or about curious and glorious achievments - could have whole chapters in regard to the Founders, and in regard to their allies and friends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-15T01:17:14-07:00","id":1511700,"title":"","content":"Would be awesome, thats for sure<br /> Most of the Ancients are loaded with historical goodies <br /> One of my personal favorites - as a curve ball - how Sutekh became &quot;God&quot;; In the earliest Biblical literature Yahweh was a storm god, a &quot;divine warrior&quot; who fought against the Darkness and with the heavenly host of stars and planets that make up his army to do battle with the enemies of his people Israel... Yahweh, eventually became known as Jehovah and then, simply, as \u201cGod\u201d,<br /> Sounds familiar, isn't it? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T03:27:39-07:00","id":1512272,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511164-arikel?p=1511700#post1511700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would be awesome, thats for sure<br /> Most of the Ancients are loaded with historical goodies</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is good to remeber and support that notion and the idea that the Clan Founders ( and also for example Bloodline Founders, and also Vampires who are paragons and representatives of their particular Clan ) and their activites, themes, qualities and stories are important and significant in regard to the atmosphere and concepts of Vampire: the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> In addition I would make that case that this area of Vampire: the Masquerade is definitely significant to at least some meaningful extent in regard to the complete and wider World of Darkness - distinctly contributing to the World of Darkness being a varied, positive, comprehensive and extended environment and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-13T20:42:44-07:00","id":1514913,"title":"","content":"I remember an interesting tidbit that there is a faction of Lilith followers that claim that when Caine and the 3rd gen killed Lilith and Lucifer's children, Arikel and Absimilard were the only two not to partake in it. So the group will leave members from those clans alone while hunting the others down. I wish I could remember which book I read it in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-18T10:39:52-07:00","id":1515464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511164-arikel?p=1514913#post1514913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember an interesting tidbit that there is a faction of Lilith followers that claim that when Caine and the 3rd gen killed Lilith and Lucifer's children, Arikel and Absimilard were the only two not to partake in it. So the group will leave members from those clans alone while hunting the others down. I wish I could remember which book I read it in.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in<i> Revelations of the Dark Mother</i>, in the context of a Bahari ritual that symbolically reenacts the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-use